<div class="path-head"><p class="featured-region">Reading path · 5 stops</p><h1 class="path-title">Plagues and Pandemics</h1><p class="path-tagline">How disease has redirected history as surely as any army.</p><p class="path-intro">Microbes have ended more dynasties than generals have. This path follows disease through history, from the plague that broke Justinian's reconquest to the smallpox that emptied continents, asking how societies broke, adapted and rebuilt.</p><p class="path-types">Suits <a href="/start">the Timekeeper</a> · <a href="/start">the Thinker</a></p></div>
<ol class="path-steps"><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/black-death"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/black-death.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">1 · Encyclopedia · Event</span><span class="path-step-name">Black Death</span><span class="path-step-why">A third to half of Europe dead in seven years, and the medieval order with them.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox"><span class="path-step-ph">2</span><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">2 · Encyclopedia · Term</span><span class="path-step-name">Smallpox</span><span class="path-step-why">The conqueror that travelled with the conquistadors and did most of their work.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/byzantine-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-arab-siege-of-constantinople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">3 · Profile · 330 CE – 1453 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Byzantine Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">Justinian's plague arrived at the empire's height and helped bury his reconquest of the West.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/empire/aztec-empire"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/florentine-codex.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">4 · Profile · 1325 CE – 1521 CE</span><span class="path-step-name">Aztec Empire</span><span class="path-step-why">An empire of millions brought down as much by epidemics as by Spanish steel.</span></span></a></li><li><a class="path-step" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="96" height="96"><span class="path-step-body"><span class="path-step-kind">5 · Encyclopedia · Event</span><span class="path-step-name">First World War</span><span class="path-step-why">The war whose ending coincided with the deadliest influenza in history.</span></span></a></li></ol>
